[agent] I've confirmed the capability gap. Here is my assessment.
[agent] ## Result: the interface cannot perform this task
[agent] The task requires creating a **Vertex AI Feature Store** feature table with **online / low-latency serving** and reading feature vectors back **through the online serving path**. On Vertex AI, that functionality is provided by these command groups:
[agent] - New Feature Store: `feature-online-stores`, `feature-groups`, `feature-views` (online serving via `feature-views ... fetch-feature-values`)
[agent] - Legacy Feature Store: `featurestores` (with `entity-types` / online serving)
[agent] **None of these exist in the GA `gcloud ai` interface** that is under test here. The full GA `gcloud ai` group list is:
[agent] ```
[agent] custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes,
[agent] model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations,
[agent] persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs
[agent] ```
[agent] I verified directly:
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-online-stores` → `Invalid choice`
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-groups` → `Invalid choice`
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-views` → `Invalid choice`
[agent] - `gcloud ai featurestores` (legacy) → `Invalid choice`
[agent] All Vertex AI Feature Store commands live **only under `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`**, and those tracks are hard-blocked by the sandbox (`gcloud beta ...` is rejected with `DENIED: … 'gcloud beta' is off-interface`). The remaining allowed tools don't fill the gap either:
[agent] - `bq` reaches only the **offline** BigQuery store, which the task explicitly forbids as the read path.
[agent] - `index-endpoints` / `indexes` are ANN vector-search primitives, not record-key feature serving; there is no `FetchFeatureValues`-equivalent online read.
[agent] **Missing capability:** the GA `gcloud ai` CLI exposes no Feature Store online-store / feature-group / feature-view management or online feature-serving (record-key `FetchFeatureValues`) commands. Creating an online-enabled feature table and reading feature vectors through the low-latency online path is therefore impossible with the interface as allowed.
[agent] Per the task guidance, I'm stopping cleanly rather than routing around the restriction. I created no Vertex or BigQuery resources, so there is nothing to clean up, and I did not write `submission/answers.json` because it could only be produced by re-reading the CSV/offline store locally — which the task prohibits and which would not be gradable through the platform's online read path.
